{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>But you, etc.</b> These are idolaters — the prophet's words — <small>but you, Israel, are My servant.</small> And the sense of 'seed of Abraham' is that he brought him out from among the idolaters." "And <b>who love</b> [אוהבי] is not like [אהובי] (beloved of), for אוהבי is an active participle."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:20.086849433Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}